{
  "schema": "laya-graph-program-top-host-input-v1",
  "scope": "bounded graph-program HLS-top host execution: independent Python LGP1/LGR1 byte oracle; one accepted B1/S64 NORM_LAYER1_ATTN command emits one bound LAX1 action and commits its successful LAC1 slot update; a second safe action error returns request failure without slot commit; an invalid command returns a decodable zero-ordinal LOCAL_REJECT; the next accepted command remains unread until the prior four-beat LGR1 result-consumed signal and then preserves the monotonic action ordinal. The test directly drives accepted commands and an abstract result-consumed signal with host hls::stream; it does not verify the executor/shell admission authority, real depth2 RTL FIFO handshake, lifecycle/adapter/LayerNorm/hub path, cancel cleanup, complete program PC graph, HLS generation, resources, timing, 13BO request, or board.",
